5,1,1,talk,Midori,,I’m a bit nervous about jumping straight into vendor names. Can we first agree on what actually went wrong with our last system?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. We need to identify the operational failures first. Specifically, how the current setup handles peak season and yard equipment constraints.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,Agreed. But let’s not just list problems. I want to know which ones are chronic and which are just bad luck.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I’d like to understand the human cost. How much strain did the last rollout put on our remaining staff?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I’d like to trace the money. Not the sticker price, but the recurring costs that quietly outlive the project.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that recurring cost angle is vital. @May, how do we separate chronic issues from one-off bad luck?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, chronic issues repeat despite fixes. Look for patterns in our upgrade history and support ownership during outages.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, good point. I’ll dig into the upgrade history and the 2018 data lift to see if those patterns hold.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, I’ll check the administrator retirements and the depot supervisors. I need to see if our people can actually absorb another change.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll examine the board minutes and the renewal invoices. I need to see if the budget actually reflects the long-term reality we’re facing.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,I’ll look into the support ownership during the last outage and the warehouse rule changes. I need to see if responsibility is clear and if our plans actually stick.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
