35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found the support was unowned for two days last winter. Also, our frozen scope broke within a year. We need a single point of accountability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The November freeze is a hard constraint. Our yard devices are outdated, and the 2021 trial failed. Any solution must work with our current hardware and calendar.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,Three skipped upgrades and a year of broken data. We keep patching rot instead of fixing it.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Two admins retire this year, and the last hire took eleven months. Plus, supervisors ignored the last rollout’s training. We are dangerously thin on people.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The board trims capital but ignores operating costs. Invoices show bundled deals stay flat, while add-ons climb yearly. We are funding the leak, not the fix.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that confirms my fear. We need a vendor who owns the whole system, not just pieces. @Ryuji, does their hardware support our current yard devices?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, that is the critical question. Our yard hardware is a patchwork of older models. Any vendor must guarantee compatibility with these specific devices, or the rollout will fail immediately.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, that’s the trap. We can’t force new hardware on old yards. We need a vendor who adapts to our mess, not one that demands a clean slate.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, the supervisors dropped the last training within weeks. If we bring in a partner for training, will they actually stick, or just leave us with a manual?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, that’s the human leak. @Midori, your single point of accountability is exactly what the invoices say we’ve been avoiding.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, that is a fair worry. I want a partner who stays through the chaos, not just the launch. @Benjamin, your point about bundled costs is key.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, you’re right. We cannot force new hardware. The vendor must adapt to our existing, aging yard devices, or the rollout fails immediately.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, exactly. We need a vendor who respects our aging hardware, not one demanding a clean slate. @Midori, your single point of accountability is the only way to stop the rot.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, if the partner leaves, we are back to square one. I need to know who stays to support the supervisors when the trainers pack up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, exactly. The invoices prove we pay for the pieces, not the whole. We need a single throat to choke when the add-ons start climbing again.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, I hear you. We need a vendor who stays through the chaos, not just the launch. @Benjamin, your point about bundled costs is key.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
